@startuml
title Diagnostic to intelligence flow - target, not current runtime
actor User
rectangle "Diagnostic inputs\nand evidence" as input
rectangle "Measurements and signals\n(optional normalisation)" as signal
rectangle "Diagnostic rules,\nderived signals and insights" as diagnostic
rectangle "Maturity evidence projection and\nsemantic engine (isolated, not UI-integrated)" as maturity
rectangle "Role Profile Builder and profiles\nfuture, not prerequisite" as profiles
rectangle "Operational MRI:\nscopes, relationships and dimensions" as mri
rectangle "Evaluate evidence, confidence,\nsignificance and priority" as evaluation
rectangle "Compose and decide presentation" as output
rectangle "Shared Intelligence Trace\n(target contract)" as trace
rectangle "Diagnostics Console" as console
User --> input
input --> signal
input --> diagnostic : direct evidence
signal --> diagnostic
input --> maturity : direct selections
input ..> profiles : future
profiles ..> maturity : future interpreted evidence
maturity --> diagnostic : diagnostic findings and evidence
input --> mri : retained evidence
signal --> mri
diagnostic --> mri
diagnostic --> evaluation
mri --> evaluation
evaluation --> output
output --> User : grounded narrative
input ..> trace
signal ..> trace
maturity ..> trace
diagnostic ..> trace
mri ..> trace
evaluation ..> trace
output ..> trace
trace --> console : recorded data
note bottom of trace
  Target lifecycle includes quality, provenance,
  support/challenge, evaluation and presentation states.
  Pipeline stages produce records; the console renders them.
  Current SignalTraceService covers only part of this lifecycle.
end note
note bottom of profiles
  Profiles are a future role-level user experience
  and evidence source, not a replacement for selections.
end note
@enduml
